  "claims": [
    "The actual recOf/recH map is the Artin map followed by the displayed sign-swap isomorphism; it is surjective.",
    "Canonical primitive Dirichlet characters match the source primVal at every positive integer, including ramified primes; only the trivial group character is principal.",
    "The first and second additive sign characters induce the primitive Legendre characters modulo d and q, respectively, and their product has conductor qd.",
    "The actual GPsi equality contains the full corrected principal sum and the actual nonprincipal logarithmic derivative.",
    "ThinScales and the source char_at transport apply to every character, including the principal one, at every sampled y at least Xprime/3.",
    "Finite character orthogonality directly proves positivity already for abstract inertia-coset means; actual arithmetic realization is needed to identify the analytic functions."
  ],
